"""
Deterministic checks that compare each translated procedure (out/jax/<proc>.py)
against its Fortran source (out/procedures/<proc>.F90). These catch the
"paraphrased translation" bug classes found during earlier driver repairs
WITHOUT running any code:

  FAIL-level (gate):
    lut-indices    : the set of proc_from_LUT_*(ind, ...) column indices used
                     per LUT function must match the Fortran's set
                     (caught: M2 — f1pr number used as table column)
    calls-invoked  : every procedure the Fortran calls (call statements ∪ the
                     frontend's calls list) is invoked in the translation body
                     as X( / X_core( / X_value( (caught 2026-08-25:
                     impose_max_Ni imported, never called)

  WARN-level (report, no gate — waivable):
    labelled-blocks: every Fortran labelled construct (name: if/do/select…)
                     is mentioned somewhere in the translation (caught
                     2026-08-25: k_loop_fz homogeneous freezing, calc_HM)
    zero-forever   : a variable the Fortran computes with a real expression is
                     only ever assigned a zero constant in the translation
                     (caught: M1 — qcnuc/ncnuc never computed)
    intent-out     : Fortran intent(out) arguments should be re-initialized at
                     translation entry (caught: M8 — prt_* accumulation)
    missing-consts : numeric literals present in the Fortran body but absent
                     from the translation (caught: KK2000/Cooper constants)

  INFO-level:
    invented-consts: literals in the translation absent from the Fortran
    conventions    : level/index convention claims found in docstrings
                     (e.g. "kbot=1 ... kdir=1") for manual cross-check
                     against the caller (caught: M7 — sedimentation no-op)

Waivers: out/issues/semantic_audit_waivers.json
    { "<proc>": { "<check>": ["name-or-value", ...] } }

Outputs: out/issues/semantic_audit/<proc>.json + _summary.json
Exit code 2 iff any FAIL-level finding remains after waivers.

GATE: _summary.json is what workflow_translator/audit_gate.py inspects before
runtime validation (Step 4) may be recorded or submitted — it must be newer
than every out/jax/<proc>.py and have total_fail == 0. Re-run this script
after every translation fix.
"""
